# Public documentation

This repository is public. Anyone can read the tree, the history, issues, and pull requests. Write docs, commits, comments, and examples as if they will stay public.

A block quote is a line that starts with `>`. The author wrote those lines, including the tone and the first person. Leave a block quote unchanged. Do not rephrase it, apply the tone rules to it, or move its wording into the surrounding prose. Update a block quote only when the user explicitly asks for that quote to be changed.

## No personal data

Do not commit personal data or secrets. That includes names, email addresses, phone numbers, account handles, home directories, hostnames, serial numbers, local network addresses, tokens, keys, passwords, and private URLs. Logs, screenshots, and sample output follow the same rule.

Use a placeholder instead: `~/.favlo`, `127.0.0.1`, `example-model`. If a secret was committed, remove it and rotate it. Deleting the file in a later commit leaves it in history.

## Official base models

A pipeline note names the official base model and its Hugging Face model card. A finetune, merge, or other derived checkpoint stays out of `docs/<pipeline>/`, even when this repo quantizes or serves that derived checkpoint.

The directory stem in the note is the official repository name plus the weight quants, such as `Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-fp4`. The card link is the publisher's repository, such as `Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B`.

## Tone and shape

Use calm, neutral sentences. State what the project does and what the reader can run. Skip slogans, urgency, and notes about a particular machine.

Outside a block quote, a claim by the author is in the third person. Write "the author", not "I", "me", or "my".

A public README says what the project is, how to install it, one minimal command, the license, and where to report a problem. Keep the as-built detail in linked docs such as ARCHITECTURE.md. Prefer relative links between files in the repo.

## Examples

Wrong: "Fixed the crash on the user's M5 at `/Users/user/Models`. Email me at user@example.com."

Right: "The server listens on `127.0.0.1:8000`. A missing checkpoint path is reported and the process exits."

Wrong, outside a block quote: "I admire this work, and I recommend it before trying Favlo."

Right, outside a block quote: "The author admires this work and recommends it before trying Favlo." A block quote that already says this in the first person stays as written.

Wrong: "Quantize writes `models/Example-Model-Uncensored-fp4` from `ExampleOrg/Example-Model-Uncensored`."

Right: "Quantize writes `models/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-fp4`. The model card is [Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B)."
